  "app.voiceSettings.port.cancelHint": "Cancelling costs nothing and frees you to forward or buy instead — which is what most people should do anyway.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.forwarded.label": "Keep my number, forward missed calls",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.forwarded.blurb": "You keep the number that's on your van. Calls you don't pick up ring through to the receptionist instead of voicemail.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.forwarded.caveat": "This rents a second line for the receptionist to answer on — that's the monthly charge, and it's the number your forwarding code points at. You keep giving out your own. You set the forwarding on your own phone, and you can turn it off the same way in under a minute.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.purchased.label": "Get a new number",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.purchased.blurb": "A separate line for the receptionist. Good for ads, or a second trade you want to track on its own.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.purchased.caveat": "It's a new number, so it won't catch calls to the one you already advertise.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.ported.label": "Move my number over",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.ported.blurb": "Your existing number transfers to us permanently. Nothing to forward, and one number to manage.",
  "app.voiceSettings.source.ported.caveat": "Two to four weeks, and the timing is your old carrier's to control. Most people should forward instead — it's the same result, today, and reversible.",
